{{!
    @template local_coursegen/template_activity_chooser

    The activity-type picker grid shown inside #tplActivityChooserModal, limited
    to the template's admin-allowed activity types (get_template_structure's
    allowedactivities). Mirrors core_course's real activity chooser cards
    (course/templates/local/activitychooser/item.mustache) so the loaded Boost
    theme styles the icon tint and card chrome natively.

    Classes required for JS: none — data-action drives behaviour.

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-action="local_coursegen/template/add-chooser-option" on the card link
      (data-modname identifies which allowed activity was picked)

    Context variables required for this template:
    * hasactivities bool
    * activities array - modname string, displayname string, purpose string,
      iconhtml string (raw), searchkey string (lowercase displayname, for JS filtering)

    Example context (json):
    {
        "hasactivities": true,
        "activities": [
            {
                "modname": "quiz", "displayname": "Quiz", "purpose": "assessment",
                "iconhtml": "<img class=\"icon activityicon\" src=\"#\" alt=\"\">",
                "searchkey": "quiz"
            }
        ]
    }
}}
{{#hasactivities}}
{{#activities}}
<div class="option border-0 card m-1 bg-white" role="menuitem" data-search="{{searchkey}}">
  <div class="optioninfo card-body d-flex flex-column text-center p-1">
    <a href="#" class="d-flex flex-column justify-content-between flex-fill"
       data-action="local_coursegen/template/add-chooser-option" data-modname="{{modname}}">
      <div class="optionicon mt-2 mb-1 mx-auto icon-no-margin activityiconcontainer smaller {{purpose}}">
        {{{iconhtml}}}
      </div>
      <div class="optionname clamp-2">{{displayname}}</div>
    </a>
  </div>
</div>
{{/activities}}
{{/hasactivities}}
{{^hasactivities}}
<p class="text-muted small p-3 m-0">{{#str}}courseai_template_modal_empty, local_coursegen{{/str}}</p>
{{/hasactivities}}
